{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And after these things.</b> To declare the merit of Joseph: for after his master promoted him and set him as lord over his house, and he ruled over all that he possessed, as in the matter mentioned — and he saw himself as lord — his mistress sought him, and he refused." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> Once Joseph saw himself in this prosperity, he began to eat and drink and would curl his hair, and said: 'Blessed be the Place who caused me to forget my father's house.' The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: 'Your father mourns over you, and you curl your hair! Behold, your mistress will pair herself with you and cause you trouble.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:49.202649687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}